WEBVTT

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.480
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.650
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:33.650
Pun Café!

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:54.200
What the...

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:56.990
Did I order something from the internet?

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:58.720
Holed up for the Winter

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:01.220
Yes?

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:02.430
Good morning.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:04.220
Damn it, Polar Bear!

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:06.680
Polar bear <i>(shirokuma)</i>?

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:09.570
That's white sesame <i>(shirogoma)</i>.

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:12.410
Those are stripes <i>(shima shima)</i>.

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:15.430
That's someone's wife <i>(hito zuma)</i>.

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:18.570
You're so damn annoying!

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:21.070
Annoying <i>(uttoushii)</i>?

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:24.640
That's an appetizer <i>(otoushi)</i>!

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:28.230
That's a bamboo rocker <i>(shishiodoshi)</i>!

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.380
Don't make me retort 
right when I wake up!

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:33.600
Wake up <i>(neoki)</i>?

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:36.630
That's an executioner <i>(shiokinin)</i>!

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.720
That's "when life knocks you down, 
stand back up" <i>(nanakorobi yaoki)</i>!

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.260
Knock it off!

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:50.270
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:54.230
That must have been rough, Grizzly.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:56.980
I don't even care about 
being woken up anymore.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:58.210
I got used to it.

00:02:58.210 --> 00:02:59.250
Really?

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:02.890
More importantly, I've been 
wondering this for a while,

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:06.610
but isn't there something that we 
can do about Polar Bear's puns?

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:08.510
Yeah...

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:12.550
Once he says a pun, it totally 
kills the fanciness of the café.

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:13.710
Right?

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:15.750
Oh, I know!

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:18.130
What? You got a good idea?

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:20.590
How about this?

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:24.550
Puns?

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:29.790
Exactly. To show Polar Bear 
how annoying his puns are,

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:32.980
we're going to reply to everything 
he says with a pun ourselves.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.110
Sounds great! Let's do it!

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:38.660
Thank you for that quick 
reply which had absolutely

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:39.860
no thought put into it.

00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:42.450
Eh, that's fine.

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:44.520
You, too, Mr. Grizzly?

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:46.580
Sounds good to me.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:49.760
He disturbs me while I'm holed up
 for the winter every year.

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:51.910
All right! Let's do this!

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:56.000
Hey, he's back.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:01.670
I'm back.

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:04.470
I'm back <i>(tadaima)</i>?

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.510
Freshly picked!

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:08.420
Oh, are they taro potatoes <i>(taroimo)</i>?

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:12.200
Hey, you look fat and delicious.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:15.150
I think "climber" would have worked 
better than a black cayman <i>(kurokaiman)</i>.

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:19.630
Greengrocer

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:18.900
What the hell?! There are 
bugs all over this!

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:19.920
A complainer <i>(kureima)</i>?

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:24.320
A color timer <i>(taima)</i>?

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:28.330
Hold on. Let's take 
a break for a second.

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:30.830
Take a break <i>(kyuukei)</i>?

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:32.870
Acrobatics <i>(kyokugei)</i>!

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:35.080
Keukenhof Park <i>(kyukenhofu kouen)</i>...

00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:38.450
How should I express that?

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:39.960
What the heck is that?

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:41.640
It's a park in Holland.

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:43.510
It's break <i>(kyuukei)</i>, right?

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:46.200
Break, break <i>(kyuukei, kyuukei)</i>...

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:48.250
Life sentence <i>(mukikyuukei)</i>!

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:50.810
Prosecutor

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:50.810
Judge

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:52.830
Take that, Polar Bear!

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:55.640
Now you know how it feels to have 
someone making puns all the time!

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:58.520
Think <i>(kangaeru)</i>?

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:00.270
Kangaroo <i>(kangaruu)</i>.

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:02.600
Take me home

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:02.320
Cardboard box <i>(danboru)</i>.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:04.610
Man hole <i>(man hooru)</i>.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:06.820
Gateball <i>(geeto booru)</i>.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.950
Damn it! Don't let him beat us!

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:14.540
Why don't you give up already?

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.120
Give up <i>(kousan)</i>?

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.680
Hey, Penguin! Think of something!

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:21.170
What?! Me?

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:24.060
Um... Um...

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:26.310
It doesn't matter if it's a bit forced.

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:28.180
Give up, give up <i>(kousan, kousan)</i>...

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.530
Namu ami da—

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:32.590
A monk <i>(bousan)</i>.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:33.960
Mass production <i>(ryousan)</i>.

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:35.770
Dad <i>(tousan)</i>!

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:37.600
Elephant <i>(zousan)</i>.

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:41.550
3+3+7 time signature 
<i>(San san nana byoshi)</i>!

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:51.670
That last one was rather forced.

00:05:51.670 --> 00:05:52.660
Forced <i>(gouin)</i>?

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:54.890
Hospital <i>(byouin)</i>.

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:56.790
Drive-thru <i>(doraibuin)</i>.

00:05:57.970 --> 00:05:58.880
Throw in <i>(surooin)</i>.

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:00.970
Flooring <i>(furooringu)</i>.

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:02.710
Worldly man <i>(kurounin)</i>.

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:04.880
Heavy drinking <i>(bouin)</i>.

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:06.760
Lowly, masterless samurai <i>(surounin)</i>.

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:08.770
Protein <i>(purotein)</i>.

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:10.720
Heroine <i>(hiroin)</i>.

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:13.680
Heroine? Um...

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:15.470
Wedding reception <i>(hirouen)</i>.

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:18.060
Meow <i>(goronyan)</i>.

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:20.730
Um, meow...

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:23.070
Coin laundry <i>(koin randorii)</i>.

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:25.060
Park <i>(kouen)</i>.

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:27.060
Does that work?

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:29.280
Funeral gift <i>(kouden)</i>.

00:06:29.850 --> 00:06:31.950
You keep straying from 
the word. No fair.

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:34.160
No fair <i>(zuruina)</i>.

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:36.290
Sausage <i>(uinnaa)</i>.

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:39.580
Don't try 
this at home, 
kids.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.580
Frankensteiner <i>(furankenshutaina)</i>.

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:42.340
Hold on a second. Time.

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:43.530
Time <i>(taimu)</i>?

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:46.840
Mayim Mayim <i>(maimu maimu)</i>!

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:48.340
Huh?

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.050
Where'd Polar Bear go?

00:06:55.730 --> 00:06:57.520
Good grief...

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:03.140
Welcome!

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:05.190
I'm beat.

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:06.980
Could I get a caffè latte?

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:09.570
Caffè latte <i>(kafue rate)</i>?

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:11.260
Push ups <i>(udetate)</i>?

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:14.120
Hakodate.

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:16.330
Huh?

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:19.000
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:26.230
What's the matter?

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:28.710
Oh, Anteater.

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:31.640
I was at Lesser Panda's and...

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:32.590
Lesser panda <i>(ressaa panda)</i>?

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:35.930
Heave-ho <i>(essa hoisa)</i>!

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:40.390
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:45.020
Oh?

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:46.020
Oh, Tortoise.

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:48.950
Tortoise <i>(zougame)</i>?

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:51.780
Solingen <i>(zouringen)</i>!

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:54.780
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:07:58.590 --> 00:07:59.790
What's wrong?

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:04.420
Oh, Mr. Handa.

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:06.800
Are you all right?

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:09.760
Would you like to get some tea?

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:12.970
Sure.

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:14.130
Tea

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:17.870
What happened?

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:21.770
Everyone keeps making puns.

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:23.590
Puns?

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:25.540
Puns...

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:28.870
Please wait one moment. 
I'll think of one quickly.

00:08:30.700 --> 00:08:32.150
Not you, too, Mr. Handa?!

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:35.160
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:42.710
I'm sorry for all of the 
trouble that I have caused.

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:46.540
I'll make sure not to say anymore puns.

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:48.730
About that.

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:51.380
Maybe puns aren't so bad after all.

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:53.050
Huh?

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:57.140
They sort of became fun to say.

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:58.010
Yeah.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:04.100
Oh, whatever. They suit you.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:05.840
He's right.

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:07.940
Puns are pretty neat.

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:15.230
Oh, that's right.

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:18.450
Since we're on the subject...

00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:23.790
Mr. Penguin, your "life 
sentence" pun doesn't work.

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:27.370
Also, during the "forced" 
pun, Grizzly, your

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:30.460
"meow" was way too forced.

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:33.930
On second thought,

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:37.100
let's ban Polar Bear from using puns.

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:38.550
Yeah.

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:40.430
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:42.560
All Kinds 
of Parfaits

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:44.310
Suddenly 
Bamboo

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:45.680
Salmon 
Left Behind

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:49.940
Black 
Bear's 
Café

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:57.630
The Secret to Delicious Coffee

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:57.620
The secret to...

00:09:57.620 --> 00:09:59.390
delicious coffee!

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:12.040
Oh, you don't have to do 
that, Master. I'll make it.

00:10:14.150 --> 00:10:16.470
Sometimes I want to do it myself.

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:25.040
Does the taste change depending 
on how you prepare it?

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:28.590
The Red Squirrels all say

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:32.840
my coffee isn't good enough yet.

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:34.620
You still have a ways to go.

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:36.900
There are a lot of factors.

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:38.110
Factors?

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:41.350
Where the beans came from, 
how they're roasted,

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:43.830
how they're ground, if the 
ground is fine or course...

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:45.910
The temperature of the hot water.

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:50.000
Pouring the water in slowly,

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:55.050
or pouring it in quickly.

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:06.430
It's true! They're totally different!

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:13.300
I get that it tastes different 
 depending on how you prepare it,

00:11:13.300 --> 00:11:14.480
but there seems to be a lot to it...

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:17.890
I wonder how long it'll 
take for the Red Squirrels

00:11:17.890 --> 00:11:19.500
to tell me my coffee's delicious.

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:22.550
So you want them to say 
that it's delicious?

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:23.950
Of course!

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:27.040
I know of a good way.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:30.040
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:31.500
Here you go.

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:33.290
Oh, truffles?

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:36.140
How thoughtful of you, Masaki.

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:38.880
Sweets are great when you're tired.

00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:44.470
Hey, do you have our coffee, yet?

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:45.310
Oh, right.

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:49.180
Here you go.

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:54.230
Oh!

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:56.050
This is...

00:11:56.050 --> 00:11:56.970
Indeed.

00:11:59.970 --> 00:12:01.240
Have them eat something sweet

00:12:01.930 --> 00:12:03.490
before they drink the coffee.

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:05.570
Huh? That's it?

00:12:06.130 --> 00:12:07.850
Well, just give it a shot.

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:10.650
This is good, considering 
it's your coffee.

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:11.830
It really is.

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:13.750
Maybe you've finally grown, Masaki.

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:16.230
All right!

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:18.670
Hey, get off your high horse.

00:12:18.980 --> 00:12:20.940
But it was good, right?

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:24.290
But I want to drink something 
a little more full-bodied.

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:26.180
You're too picky!

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:29.970
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:34.900
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:33.730
Mr. Full-Time Panda, 
Mr. Llama and Rin Rin!

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:36.690
Internet
Comics & Games

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:43.140
Hey, Mr. Full-Time.

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:45.050
What is it, Panda?

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:47.210
Are you going to help me?

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:48.490
Not a chance.

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:52.440
You always answer so bluntly, Panda.

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:54.330
So, what did you want?

00:12:55.220 --> 00:12:59.120
I'm tired of lazing around, 
so I'm gonna leave early.

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:01.810
Would you punch my time card for me?

00:13:02.390 --> 00:13:07.020
What? I'm the one who'd like to do that.

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:11.310
If you can't do it, 
I guess I'll ask Mr. Handa.

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:13.890
Absolutely not.

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:16.150
No matter what?

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:18.310
Of course!

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:22.920
No heated tables 
or side-jobs allowed!

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:29.280
At this rate, I won't be able 
to seriously lay around.

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:31.890
It can't be helped, Panda.

00:13:32.470 --> 00:13:33.870
At times like these...

00:13:34.590 --> 00:13:35.290
What?

00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:37.000
Let's go to sleep.

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:40.500
If we go to sleep, it'll be 
closing time before you know it.

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:44.300
Yeah! You're right.

00:13:45.870 --> 00:13:48.470
All pandas have to do is sleep!

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:53.180
Panda,

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:55.740
let's play with the tire.

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:59.020
The zoo is now closing.

00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:02.290
Please visit again.

00:14:09.510 --> 00:14:14.210
Man, you should have woken 
me up, Mr. Full-Time.

00:14:14.210 --> 00:14:18.250
You were sleeping so soundly. 
I'll punch your card for you.

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:23.080
Hey, it's me. I'm heading home.

00:14:23.890 --> 00:14:26.000
You can go ahead and 
take a bath before me.

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:27.840
Bye.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:30.140
Call Time

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:32.840
Oh, hello.

00:14:32.840 --> 00:14:33.970
Thanks for all your hard work.

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:37.690
Do you want to walk to 
the station together?

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:44.400
I keep wondering how long I'm going 
to be able to continue this job.

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:46.860
Makes me think about the future.

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:47.900
I totally understand.

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:52.360
I keep wondering if I should 
keep working as a llama or not.

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:56.060
Oh, Mr. Llama,
 you're fine as a llama.

00:14:57.040 --> 00:15:00.330
Zoo Station

00:14:58.240 --> 00:15:00.330
Looks like we got to the station.

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:04.090
Should we go straight home?

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:07.010
Bird Land

00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:08.970
Cheers!

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:12.130
Man, this makes me happy.

00:15:12.130 --> 00:15:13.900
Indeed.

00:15:13.900 --> 00:15:16.930
Come on, drink up. Drink up.

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:20.440
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:15:20.900 --> 00:15:21.610
Thirty-six...

00:15:23.490 --> 00:15:24.900
skewers.

00:15:25.490 --> 00:15:28.140
9x4 <i>(ku-shi)</i> is 36 and you 
have 36 skewers <i>(kushi)</i>?

00:15:29.870 --> 00:15:32.460
You're a riot, Mr. Llama.

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:35.820
Really? I get told I'm quite dull.

00:15:35.820 --> 00:15:38.060
Not dull at all! Quite flashy, really.

00:15:38.060 --> 00:15:40.370
Oh, not at all.

00:15:41.050 --> 00:15:44.510
It doesn't make any sense that 
you're not popular, Mr. Llama.

00:15:44.510 --> 00:15:47.110
You bring that Alpaca here.

00:15:47.450 --> 00:15:50.380
I'll tell him a thing or two.

00:15:50.910 --> 00:15:52.950
Oh, the thought itself 
is more than enough.

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:55.650
One more glass, Mr. Full-Time?

00:15:55.650 --> 00:15:57.430
Why, thank you.

00:15:57.430 --> 00:16:00.930
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:16:01.510 --> 00:16:02.900
Cheers!

00:16:04.260 --> 00:16:05.650
Why am I here?

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:07.380
Oh, come on.

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:10.680
We three just can't catch a break, so let's drink up.

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:12.120
I'm not really...

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:14.620
Oh, don't be like that.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:21.040
It's pretty slow today.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:22.290
Indeed.

00:16:23.360 --> 00:16:25.420
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:27.000
What is it, Panda?

00:16:27.660 --> 00:16:29.960
If you're bored from the 
slowness, on Saturday,

00:16:30.470 --> 00:16:32.840
you should totally go to work in my place.

00:16:33.070 --> 00:16:34.710
I can't seem to find

00:16:34.710 --> 00:16:37.350
the connection between 
me being bored right now

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:39.020
and me going into work for you.

00:16:39.020 --> 00:16:40.740
Where's Polar Bear today?

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:42.540
He said he was going 
to be out for a while.

00:16:46.050 --> 00:16:47.520
It's so slow.

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:49.540
Indeed.

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:52.640
I'm a little hungry, so would it be

00:16:52.640 --> 00:16:55.750
okay if I borrowed the kitchen to 
make some tea over rice?

00:16:55.750 --> 00:16:57.650
Please don't.

00:16:59.090 --> 00:17:00.230
Over here!

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:04.480
You okay, Mr. Llama?

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:06.660
I'm fine.

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:08.340
Are we there yet, Mr. Hayashi?

00:17:12.160 --> 00:17:14.260
Is this place really okay?

00:17:14.640 --> 00:17:15.980
Let's go in!

00:17:16.360 --> 00:17:19.970
Don't worry! 
Leave the fierce beasts to me!

00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:21.680
Welcome.

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:26.020
Oh, Mr. Polar Bear. 
Where's Otter today?

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:29.480
Otter said it was his 
girlfriend's birthday today,

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:30.800
so I'm working for him.

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:35.240
Well, this is an unusual group.

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:39.720
What's so unusual about us? 
We're all friends!

00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:42.750
Man, I'm so happy!

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:47.470
Indeed. Do you come here 
often, Mr. Hayashi?

00:17:47.470 --> 00:17:49.590
Every now and then when 
I want to have a drink.

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:53.090
Man, young people are so fancy.

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:57.290
I only ever go to
 yakitori restaurants and such,

00:17:57.290 --> 00:17:59.550
so just setting foot in a place 
like this gets me drunk.

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:03.160
Well, and I'm already drunk.

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:04.520
So much fun.

00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:09.360
Hey, where are all the 
fierce beasts tonight?

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:12.920
I hope that the fierce 
beasts get here soon!

00:18:12.920 --> 00:18:14.500
It's fine if they're not here.

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:16.890
We can relax and drink 
if they're not here.

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:19.370
So true.

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:23.730
Man, we're so awesome!

00:18:24.280 --> 00:18:28.030
I know! Let's just run 
a zoo all by ourselves!

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:30.130
Let's do it, Mr. Hayashi!

00:18:30.490 --> 00:18:33.420
What? I somehow got included, too?

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:34.630
You bet you did.

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:39.340
It'll belong to just us: 
me, Mr. Llama and Run Run!

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:40.510
It's Rin Rin.

00:18:41.190 --> 00:18:43.260
We'll get lots of visitors!

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:44.540
You think so?

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:46.520
Yeah! That sounds awesome! Woo!

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:48.230
You can join us, too, Polar Bear.

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:50.440
Oh, hold on one second.

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:04.380
What?

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:08.200
Mr. Full-Time Panda 
and Mr. Llama are here

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:10.090
drinking at Grizzly's Bar right now.

00:19:10.090 --> 00:19:11.100
Wanna join us?

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:12.550
I'm hanging up.

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:15.210
He hung up on me.

00:19:15.660 --> 00:19:20.450
And I totally thought about including 
Grizzly in your zoo, too.

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:23.260
It'll be fine with just the four of us.

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:28.270
My Zoo

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:28.270
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:31.100
Let's open up some champagne.

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:33.020
Sounds great.

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:36.690
You sure? I'll drink it all up.

00:19:37.750 --> 00:19:40.280
I'm wide awake now, damn it.

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:42.810
Hey! It's a fierce beast!

00:19:42.810 --> 00:19:44.470
Hey, fierce beast!

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:47.060
There's a seat for you right here.

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:50.290
Yeah, they're drunk.

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:54.790
Oh, Grizzly, I just opened 
up a bottle of champagne.

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:57.280
I can put it on the store's tab, right?

00:19:57.280 --> 00:19:59.170
Why the hell are you opening 
that without permission?!

00:20:00.410 --> 00:20:02.660
Well then, I think I'll head home.

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:05.920
Bourbon, on the rocks.

00:20:06.280 --> 00:20:08.520
What? I have to do it?

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:10.640
You're the one who woke me up.

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:12.550
Oh, all right.

00:20:16.140 --> 00:20:18.240
It was salmon and mackerel, right?

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:21.360
Bourbon on the rocks! 
Damn, you're annoying.

00:20:22.440 --> 00:20:23.320
Here you go.

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:26.090
Now that's the stuff.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:30.660
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:34.040
You guys...

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:37.150
are totally awesome!

00:20:37.150 --> 00:20:40.690
All right! Let's all go motorcycle touring!

00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:42.000
Sounds good.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:44.270
You can ride a bike, Full-Time?

00:20:44.270 --> 00:20:47.350
I don't have a license 
so let me ride in back.

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:49.430
Sounds good!

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:51.670
I wonder if I can ride a bike.

00:20:51.670 --> 00:20:54.510
You just have to force yourself on.

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:56.530
Gotcha.

00:20:56.530 --> 00:20:59.200
Mr. Polar Bear, could I get 
another? The same thing.

00:20:59.200 --> 00:21:01.220
I want another, too.

00:21:01.220 --> 00:21:02.310
Me, too!

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:04.950
Whatcha drinkin', Full-Time?

00:21:05.980 --> 00:21:07.470
Shochu with hot water.

00:21:07.470 --> 00:21:10.110
We don't serve that here. 
You're way too drunk.

00:21:10.570 --> 00:21:12.610
Oh well, whatever. 
I'll have one, too.

00:21:12.610 --> 00:21:13.950
Here you go. 
Want some pickled plums in it?

00:21:13.950 --> 00:21:16.790
Where the hell did you get that from?

00:21:17.190 --> 00:21:19.230
Oh, hey. What's going on here?

00:21:19.230 --> 00:21:20.750
Looks like quite the party tonight.

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:22.430
Hey!

00:21:22.430 --> 00:21:24.900
Oh my! More fierce beasts!

00:21:24.900 --> 00:21:26.570
We're totally open over here!

00:21:26.570 --> 00:21:29.050
Come on over! Come, on, over!

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:30.100
Thanks.

00:21:32.780 --> 00:21:34.500
Come on, one more!

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:35.390
Well, thank you.

00:21:35.790 --> 00:21:38.660
And so, this is what I think...

00:21:38.660 --> 00:21:39.730
Yeah.

00:21:40.310 --> 00:21:42.320
Quite the lively crew tonight...

00:21:42.320 --> 00:21:43.630
Oh, welcome back.

00:21:43.630 --> 00:21:47.200
Hey, Otter! You need to drink, too!

00:22:14.560 --> 00:22:15.230
Oh?

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:25.090
Next Time

00:23:58.150 --> 00:23:59.630
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.630 --> 00:24:00.700
What is it, Panda?

00:24:00.700 --> 00:24:02.100
Next week's Polar Bear's Café...

00:24:02.100 --> 00:24:02.780
You're early!

00:24:02.780 --> 00:24:04.340
Way too early!

00:24:04.340 --> 00:24:07.000
Can't you even wait twenty 
seconds, Polar Bear?

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:09.210
Sorry. I'll be waiting quietly, then.

00:24:08.570 --> 00:24:10.940
[Polar Bear is dressed as the Kumamoto mascot Kumamon.]

00:24:09.210 --> 00:24:10.920
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:10.920 --> 00:24:11.880
Hey, hold on a second!

00:24:11.880 --> 00:24:13.600
How can you let it end like this?

00:24:13.600 --> 00:24:15.880
We don't need your assertiveness 
right now, Panda.

00:24:15.880 --> 00:24:17.390
What's wrong, Polar Bear?

00:24:17.390 --> 00:24:19.280
Next week's Polar Bear's Café,

00:24:19.280 --> 00:24:20.730
will be brought to you 
as soon as I wake up.

00:24:20.730 --> 00:24:21.850
It'll be fun!

00:24:21.850 --> 00:24:24.000
Not you, too, Miss Sasako!

00:24:21.890 --> 00:24:24.800
The Everyday Zoo
The Zoo in the Rain
